Also, the altitude $AD$ bisects $BC$, so $BD = CD$. Let $CD = x$. Then $BC = BD + CD = x + x = 2x$. Since $BC=5$, we have $2x=5$, so $x = 2.5$. Thus $CD = 2.5$.
Now, we want to find the area of $\triangle DEC$. We have $CE = 3$ and $CD = 2.5$.
