We have the determinant of the matrix
\[
A = \begin{pmatrix} \sec^2 x & 1 & 1 \\ \cos^2 x & \cos^2 x & \csc^2 x \\ 1 & \cos^2 x & \cot^2 x \end{pmatrix}.
\]
We want to find the value of $\det(A)$ as $x$ ranges over all real numbers.
We can expand the determinant along the first row:
\begin{align*} \det(A) &= \sec^2 x \begin{vmatrix} \cos^2 x & \csc^2 x \\ \cos^2 x & \cot^2 x \end{vmatrix} - 1 \begin{vmatrix} \cos^2 x & \csc^2 x \\ 1 & \cot^2 x \end{vmatrix} + 1 \begin{vmatrix} \cos^2 x & \cos^2 x \\ 1 & \cos^2 x \end{vmatrix} \\ &= \sec^2 x (\cos^2 x \cot^2 x - \csc^2 x \cos^2 x) - ( \cos^2 x \cot^2 x - \csc^2 x ) + (\cos^4 x - \cos^2 x) \\ &= \sec^2 x (\cos^2 x \frac{\cos^2 x}{\sin^2 x} - \frac{1}{\sin^2 x} \cos^2 x) - \cos^2 x \frac{\cos^2 x}{\sin^2 x} + \frac{1}{\sin^2 x} + \cos^4 x - \cos^2 x \\ &= \sec^2 x \left( \frac{\cos^4 x}{\sin^2 x} - \frac{\cos^2 x}{\sin^2 x} \right) - \frac{\cos^4 x}{\sin^2 x} + \frac{1}{\sin^2 x} + \cos^4 x - \cos^2 x \\ &= \frac{\sec^2 x}{\sin^2 x} (\cos^4 x - \cos^2 x) - \frac{\cos^4 x}{\sin^2 x} + \frac{1}{\sin^2 x} + \cos^4 x - \cos^2 x \end{align*}
This seems too complicated.
Let's try expanding along the second row:
\begin{align*} \det(A) &= -\cos^2 x \begin{vmatrix} 1 & 1 \\ \cot^2 x & \cot^2 x \end{vmatrix} + \csc^2 x \begin{vmatrix} \sec^2 x & 1 \\ 1 & \cot^2 x \end{vmatrix} - \csc^2 x \begin{vmatrix} \sec^2 x & 1 \\ 1 & \cos^2 x \end{vmatrix} \\ &= -\cos^2 x ( \cot^2 x - \cot^2 x ) + \csc^2 x ( \sec^2 x \cot^2 x - 1 ) - \csc^2 x ( \sec^2 x \cos^2 x - \cos^2 x ) \\ &= 0 + \csc^2 x (\sec^2 x \cot^2 x - 1) - \csc^2 x ( \sec^2 x \cos^2 x - \cos^2 x ) \\ &= \csc^2 x (\sec^2 x \cot^2 x - 1 - \sec^2 x \cos^2 x + \cos^2 x ) \end{align*}
This also seems complicated.

Let's expand along the third row:
\begin{align*} \det(A) &= 1 \begin{vmatrix} 1 & 1 \\ \cos^2 x & \csc^2 x \end{vmatrix} - \cos^2 x \begin{vmatrix} \sec^2 x & 1 \\ \cos^2 x & \csc^2 x \end{vmatrix} + \cot^2 x \begin{vmatrix} \sec^2 x & 1 \\ \cos^2 x & \cos^2 x \end{vmatrix} \\ &= 1 (\csc^2 x - \cos^2 x) - \cos^2 x ( \sec^2 x \csc^2 x - \cos^2 x ) + \cot^2 x ( \sec^2 x \cos^2 x - \cos^2 x ) \\ &= \csc^2 x - \cos^2 x - \cos^2 x \sec^2 x \csc^2 x + \cos^4 x + \cot^2 x \sec^2 x \cos^2 x - \cot^2 x \cos^2 x \\ &= \csc^2 x - \cos^2 x - \cos^2 x \frac{1}{\cos^2 x} \frac{1}{\sin^2 x} + \cos^4 x + \frac{\cos^2 x}{\sin^2 x} \frac{1}{\cos^2 x} \cos^2 x - \frac{\cos^2 x}{\sin^2 x} \cos^2 x \\ &= \csc^2 x - \cos^2 x - \frac{1}{\sin^2 x} + \cos^4 x + \frac{1}{\sin^2 x} - \frac{\cos^4 x}{\sin^2 x} \\ &= \csc^2 x - \cos^2 x - \frac{1}{\sin^2 x} + \cos^4 x + \frac{1}{\sin^2 x} - \frac{\cos^4 x}{\sin^2 x} \\ &= \csc^2 x - \cos^2 x + \cos^4 x - \frac{\cos^4 x}{\sin^2 x} \end{align*}

$\det(A) = 1$

