Since we are looking for seven-digit phone numbers, and the first three digits are fixed as 336, we have four digits left to choose for the middle (xxxx).  Each of these digits can be any digit from 0 to 9, so we have 10 choices for each of the four digits. Therefore, the number of possibilities for xxxx is $10 \times 10 \times 10 \times 10 = 10^4 = 10000$.

