Here is the solution:
We need to compute the matrix-vector product $\begin{pmatrix} 1 & 2 \\ 4 & 8 \\ \end{pmatrix} \begin{pmatrix} 5 \\ 3 \end{pmatrix}$. We multiply the first row with the vector:
$$ \begin{pmatrix} 1 & 2 \\ 4 & 8 \\ \end{pmatrix} \begin{pmatrix} 5 \\ 3 \end{pmatrix} = \begin{pmatrix} (1)(5) + (2)(3) \\ (4)(5) + (8)(3) \end{pmatrix} = \begin{pmatrix} 5+6 \\ 20+24 \end{pmatrix} = \begin{pmatrix} 11 \\ 44 \end{pmatrix}. $$
The result is $\begin{pmatrix} 11 \\ 44 \end{pmatrix}$.

