When $n=3$, we have $x_1 + x_2 + x_3 = 0$ and $x_1 x_2 + x_2 x_3 + x_3 x_1 \le 0$. 
Let $x_1 = 1$, $x_2 = 1$, $x_3 = -2$. Then $x_1 + x_2 + x_3 = 1 + 1 - 2 = 0$. 
$x_1 x_2 + x_2 x_3 + x_3 x_1 = (1) + (-2) + (-2) = -3 \le 0$. 
So $n=3$ is a possible value. 

