Here is the problem.
Find $\theta$, in degrees, of the smallest positive angle $\theta$ such that $\sin 3 \theta = \cos 7 \theta$.

We have $\sin 3\theta = \cos 7\theta$. Since $\sin x = \cos(90^\circ - x)$, we can write
$$\cos(90^\circ - 3\theta) = \cos 7\theta$$
This means $90^\circ - 3\theta = 7\theta + 360^\circ k$ for some integer $k$, or $90^\circ - 3\theta = -7\theta + 360^\circ k$ for some integer $k$.

Case 1: $90^\circ - 3\theta = 7\theta + 360^\circ k$
$90^\circ - 360^\circ k = 10\theta$
$\theta = \frac{90^\circ - 360^\circ k}{10} = 9^\circ - 36^\circ k$
We want the smallest positive angle $\theta$.
If $k = 0$, $\theta = 9^\circ$.
If $k = -1$, $\theta = 9^\circ + 36^\circ = 45^\circ$.
If $k = -2$, $\theta = 9^\circ + 72^\circ = 81^\circ$.
Since $9^\circ$ is the smallest positive value, $\theta = 9^\circ$.

Case 2: $90^\circ - 3\theta = -7\theta + 360^\circ k$
$90^\circ - 360^\circ k = -4\theta$
$\theta = \frac{90^\circ - 360^\circ k}{-4} = \frac{90^\circ}{-4} + \frac{360^\circ k}{4} = -22.5^\circ + 90^\circ k$
If $k = 0$, $\theta = -22.5^\circ$, which is negative.
If $k = 1$, $\theta = -22.5^\circ + 90^\circ = 67.5^\circ$.
If $k = 2$, $\theta = -22.5^\circ + 180^\circ = 157.5^\circ$.
The smallest positive angle is $67.5^\circ$.

We want the smallest positive angle $\theta$.
Comparing $9^\circ$ and $67.5^\circ$, the smallest positive angle is $9^\circ$.

Thus, $\theta = 9^\circ$.

Alternatively, using the identity $\cos(x) = \sin(90^\circ - x)$, we have
$\sin 3\theta = \sin (90^\circ - 7\theta)$.
So $3\theta = 90^\circ - 7\theta + 360^\circ k$ or $3\theta = 180^\circ - (90^\circ - 7\theta) + 360^\circ k$, for some integer $k$.
Case 1: $3\theta = 90^\circ - 7\theta + 360^\circ k$
$10\theta = 90^\circ + 360^\circ k$
$\theta = 9^\circ + 36^\circ k$
The smallest positive $\theta$ occurs when $k = 0$, so $\theta = 9^\circ$.
Case 2: $3\theta = 180^\circ - 90^\circ + 7\theta + 360^\circ k$
$3\theta = 90^\circ + 7\theta + 360^\circ k$
$-4\theta = 90^\circ + 360^\circ k$
$\theta = -22.5^\circ - 90^\circ k$
When $k = -1$, $\theta = -22.5^\circ + 90^\circ = 67.5^\circ$.
The smallest positive $\theta$ is $67.5^\circ$.

Since $9^\circ < 67.5^\circ$, the smallest positive angle $\theta$ is $9^\circ$.

