Let the side length of the cube be $s$. The volume of the cube is given by $V = s^3$. We are given that $V = 0.027$ cubic meters. So, we have $s^3 = 0.027$. Taking the cube root of both sides, we get $s = \sqrt[3]{0.027} = 0.3$ meters.

The surface area of one face of the cube is $A = s^2$. With $s = 0.3$ meters, we have $A = (0.3)^2 = 0.09$ square meters.
Since a cube has 6 faces, the total surface area of the cube is $SA = 6A = 6(0.09) = 0.54$ square meters.

