The volume of the new cube is increased by 19 cubic centimeters, so the new volume is $V_2 = V_1 + 19 = 8 + 19 = 27$ cubic centimeters.
Let the side length of the new cube be $s_2$. Then $V_2 = s_2^3$.
So, $s_2^3 = 27$.
Taking the cube root of both sides, we get $s_2 = \sqrt[3]{27} = 3$ cm.

