The volume of the small cube is $2 \text{ cm} \times 2 \text{ cm} \times 2 \text{ cm} = 8 \text{ cm}^3$.
The volume of the larger cube is $8 + 19 = 27 \text{ cm}^3$.
Let $s$ be the side length of the larger cube. Then $s^3 = 27$.
Taking the cube root of both sides, we get $s = \sqrt[3]{27} = 3 \text{ cm}$.

